# ALB is public: that's its job: users reach the app through it
AWS-0053

# HTTP, not HTTPS: HTTPS needs a domain + certificate, and there's no domain. Note it for later
AWS-0054

# ECS tasks can reach any IP: tasks must reach ECR and CloudWatch through the NAT. Locking that down needs VPC endpoints, which cost money 
# ALB can reach any IP: could be limited to the VPC. Low risk, so later
AWS-0104

# SNS topic not encrypted: CloudWatch alarms can't publish to an SNS topic that uses the free AWS key. It needs a paid KMS key (about $1/month)
AWS-0095

# state bucket uses AWS's key, not your own: it is encrypted (AES256). Your own KMS key costs about $1/month
AWS-0132